hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18996","Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Ubayd ibn Ali, from Abu Salamah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I enjoin a man concerning his mother, I enjoin a man concerning his mother, I enjoin a man concerning his mother, I enjoin a man concerning his father, I enjoin a man concerning his father, I enjoin a man concerning his client next to him, even if there is harm in it harming him."
"18997","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abdullah ibn Ali ibn Urfutah al-Sulami, from Khidash Abu Salamah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: I enjoin a person concerning his mother, I enjoin a person concerning his father, I enjoin a person concerning his mother, I enjoin a person concerning his father, I enjoin a person concerning his father, I enjoin a person concerning his client next to him, even if there is harm in it harming him."
"18998","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ubaydullah ibn Urfutah al-Sulami, from Khidash Abu Salamah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I enjoin a person, then he mentioned its meaning."
